<title>INDONESIA: Pertamina says operating profit up 853.5 bln rph.</title>
<headline>Pertamina says operating profit up 853.5 bln rph.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-02-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state-owned oil company Pertamina said its operating profit rose about 55 percent to 853.5 billion rupiah in 1995/96 against 550.8 billion rupiah in 1994/95, the company said in a statement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>Pertamina said its profit before government interest increased to 1.9 trillion rupiah in 1995/96 against 1.3 trillion rupiah in 1994/95</p>
<p>The statement said Pertamina allocated 1.0 trillion rupiah to the government in 1995/96, up from 837.8 billion rupiah in 1994/95. It gave no other details.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta Newsroom ++ 6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
